    <GaugingStation location="Invermoriston" name="Moriston" number="6003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station closed in 1945.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">The control is a broad, flat, gravel and boulder bar with a tree covered island and a steep gradient d/s. All flows contained on the left bank - the right bank is lower with a floodplain at about 3m. Peak flow rating derived from current meter gaugings (but no gaugings available).</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station. Station closed in 1945.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Because of increasing breakdowns of the recorder, records became unreliable from 1944 onwards.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural regime (reservoirs in the hydroelectric scheme began impounding in 1957, after the station was closed). Loch Loyne and Loch Cluaine were natural pre-1957.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mountainous headwaters, often snowy in winter. Pre-Cambrian grits and schists. Mainly rough pasture and moorland, some forest cover. No significant catchment changes known. Pre-reservoir FARL2015 (for WINFAP 5.3 or later) or FARL (for earlier versions of WINFAP) should be used with these records because the station closed before the reservoirs in the catchment began impounding. Pre- and post-reservoir values for FARL2015 are 0.9439 and 0.81, respectively. Pre- and post-reservoir values for FARL are 0.985 and 0.813, respectively.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="No comment." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Data quality unsure. Also out of bank flow likely for about a third of the AMAX series." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
